0..74 Comment "// A program hands the host a plan whose bound variable stands outside its"
75..115 Comment "// binder, and `admit` refuses the plan."
116..118 Comment "//"
119..193 Comment "// The root of the plan is the meet of `∀ x ∈ [0, 1] (x · x < 2)` and"
194..264 Comment "// `x < 2`, and the two comparisons share one node for `x`. Inside the"
265..341 Comment "// universal, that node is the variable that the universal binds. The second"
342..416 Comment "// comparison stands outside the universal, so there the node reaches past"
417..491 Comment "// every binder. The validation pass reads each path from the root, and it"
492..563 Comment "// refuses the plan at that node, node 1, by the check `EscapedBinder`."
564..566 Comment "//"
567..637 Comment "// `gandr run unscoped-binder.gandr` writes the refusal as one line on"
638..705 Comment "// standard error. The run stops at `admit`, and it prints nothing."
706..708 Comment "//"
709..783 Comment "// - see: `corpus/model/reals/forall.gandr` — the universal in its scope"
784..862 Comment "// - see: `crates/theory-exact-reals/src/validate.rs` — the checks of a plan"
